{"id":"q09","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"puzzle","question":"A clock takes 5 seconds to strike 6 o'clock (strikes are instantaneous and evenly spaced). Does it take 10 seconds to strike 12 o'clock?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"The clock takes 11 seconds to strike 12, not 10.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Naive proportion gives 5 s × (12/6) = 10 s.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The naive proportion wrongly treats each strike as taking a fixed share of the time.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.7,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Because strikes are instantaneous, elapsed time comes from the gaps between strikes.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Six strikes create five gaps, each lasting 1 second.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Twelve strikes create eleven gaps, totaling 11 seconds.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Total time depends on the number of intervals (n − 1), not the number of strikes (n).","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The proportional answer of 10 seconds is wrong.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":-0.9,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":-0.7,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":-0.8,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":-0.7,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"